A||N||8||Haze_Performance||The Duck is up and flying||||13||
Z||000000||Haze_Performance||04-20-2000||02:05 AM||||Today I did a Tune up on my 2M4..I guess 40,000 miles and 15 years on all the stock parts it should be time to change it all  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> . So I did the Plugs, Wires, Cap & Rotor, PCV and Fuel Filter. It was a pain in the a*s    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/mad.gif">.. The rotor was the hardest. It was stuck on so hard I thought I was going to pull the cam out with it   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif"> . My girlfriend says that there is nothing sexier looking than a greasy 6" 210lb guy stuffed in a 2-foot trunk while cursing at a motor. So I told her she looks fat in her jeans   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/tongue.gif"> . Then she left me alone.    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> SCORE ONE FOR THE GUYS   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> !! So as I was wedged in the trunk looking at the motor I noticed the heat shield under the header is loose and making alot of noise. Can I take it off and just run without it?? As I see it nothing would touch the header with it removed. I know that it is a heat shield so before I would remove it I was going to install a scoop on the decklid to help dissipate the heat... What do you guys think??   <P>[This message has been edited by Haze_Performance (edited 04-20-2000).]<p>[This message has been edited by Haze_Performance (edited 04-20-2000).]||||reg||13
Z||000001||Smokey||04-20-2000||11:26 AM||||what is with calling the 2.5 a "duck"???????<P>is it some kind of joke...or did somebody mis-spell duke somewhere along the line and now people think its a duck?||||reg||1
Z||000002||theogre||04-20-2000||11:48 AM||||No, mostly it is intentionally called that. I even do it, and I like the motor. Quack.||||reg||6
