Z||000004||Racer 1||04-20-2000||11:57 AM||||The word "<B>IRON DUCK</B>" is a perfect word and description of our 4 bangers! ||||reg||3
Z||000005||87ECO5||04-20-2000||12:21 PM||||<B>haze</B> - if I remember correctly, the heat shield under the header protects the starter from getting cooked.  Remove it and you may be visiting the local parts store every six months.<P>At least, that's what I recall hearing from someone else on here ...||||reg||1
Z||000006||GT Bastard||04-20-2000||02:50 PM||||One thing I always hated about my duck is the way it sounded.  It idled smooth with no exhaust leaks, but the exhaust note just bugged me.  It sounded like a sewing machine. ||||reg||1
Z||000007||Richard Parnell||04-20-2000||04:54 PM||||GT- If you take off the cat the 4 banger has a nice growl to it at lower speeds at higher rpms it's obvious it's a 4 banger.  I love downshifting to 1st gear and letting out the clutch as I drift up to a light, it just sounds cool.  But not as cool as the 350 will sound.||||reg||6
Z||000008||88formula||04-20-2000||09:40 PM||||Call it the IRON PUKE. The sound of the engine running sounds like someone puking.||||reg||1
